{"qid":"Q25227","names":["Netherlands Antilles"],"title":"Netherlands Antilles","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Netherlands Antilles was an autonomous country within the Kingdom of the Netherlands, constituted in 1954 under the Charter for the Kingdom as a self-governing unit comprising six Caribbean islands in two geographically separated groups: Curaçao and Bonaire (Leeward Antilles) and Sint Maarten, Sint Eustatius, and Saba (Windward Antilles), with Aruba withdrawing to separate status aparte in 1986. The federation was dissolved on 10 October 2010 after prolonged debate about its internal equity: Curaçao and Sint Maarten became autonomous constituent countries of the Kingdom, while Bonaire, Sint Eustatius, and Saba became special municipalities of the Netherlands directly. Willemstad, Curaçao, served as the administrative capital throughout the entity's existence.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Well-documented modern political entity; island boundaries are unambiguous, though the two-group geographic split made the polity non-contiguous.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Netherlands Antilles","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Netherlands-Antilles"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Netherlands Antilles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netherlands_Antilles"}],"britannica":"place/Netherlands-Antilles","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Netherlands Antilles","rulers":[{"qid":"Q6894784","name":"Moises Frumencio da Costa Gomez","start":1951,"end":1954,"image":"Moises da Costa Gomez(1960) (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Moises%20da%20Costa%20Gomez(1960)